.TH GOTTA-GO-FAST 1 "August 2026" "gotta-go-fast 0.3.0.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gotta-go-fast \- terminal utility for practicing typing and measuring WPM and accuracy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gotta-go-fast
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILES\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gotta-go-fast
is a terminal-based application written in Haskell using
.B brick
that allows users to practice typing and measure their speed (words per minute)
and accuracy.
.PP
In all modes of operation, you type through the presented target text and submit
the test with
.B ENTER
upon completion. Mistakes are highlighted as you type and \fBmust\fR be corrected
before the test can be successfully submitted. Press
.B ESC
at any time to restart the session with a new sample.
.SH MODES OF OPERATION
.B gotta-go-fast
supports three distinct modes of operation depending on command-line arguments:
.TP
.B Nonsense Mode
Invoked when no input files are provided. Generates text that is statistically similar
to English based on word frequencies. The length of generated text can be configured
using the \fB\-l\fR / \fB\-\-nonsense-len\fR option.
.TP
.B Chunk Mode
Invoked when one or more \fIFILES\fR are specified without the \fB\-p\fR / \fB\-\-paragraph\fR
flag. Samples a random chunk of lines from a randomly chosen file. The line count
can be set via \fB\-h\fR / \fB\-\-height\fR. This mode is well-suited for source code or
unstructured text files.
.TP
.B Paragraph Mode
Invoked when input \fIFILES\fR are supplied along with the \fB\-p\fR or \fB\-\-paragraph\fR
flag. Samples a random paragraph (delimited by empty lines) from a randomly selected file.
Minimum and maximum paragraph word lengths can be controlled with \fB\-\-min-paragraph-len\fR
and \fB\-\-max-paragraph-len\fR. Paragraphs can optionally be reflowed to the target width
using \fB\-r\fR / \fB\-\-reflow\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-fg\-empty= COLOUR
Set the ANSI colour code for empty (not yet typed) text (default: 8).
.TP
.BI \-\-fg\-error= COLOUR
Set the ANSI colour code for typing errors (default: 1).
.TP
.BI \-h ", " \-\-height= LINES
Maximum number of lines to sample in Chunk Mode (default: 20).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-paragraph\-len= WORDS
Maximum word count for sampled paragraphs in Paragraph Mode (default: 750).
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-paragraph\-len= WORDS
Minimum word count for sampled paragraphs in Paragraph Mode (default: 250).
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-nonsense\-len= WORDS
Number of words to generate in Nonsense Mode (default: 500).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-paragraph
Enable Paragraph Mode when sampling from input files.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reflow
Reflow paragraph text to fit the target line width in Paragraph Mode.
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-tab= SIZE
Width of tab characters expanded to spaces (default: 4).
.TP
.BI \-w ", " \-\-width= CHARS
Target line width in characters for line wrapping (default: 80).
.TP
.BR \-? ", " \-\-help
Display command help summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Printable Characters
Type target text. The timer starts automatically on the first character typed.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete the previously typed character.
.TP
.B Ctrl-w, Ctrl-Backspace, Alt-Backspace, Meta-Backspace
Delete back to the beginning of the previous word.
.TP
.B Esc
Restart the typing test with a freshly sampled text target.
.TP
.B Enter
Advance to the next line or submit the completed test (when error-free).
.TP
.B Ctrl-c, Ctrl-d
Quit the application.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Practice typing generated pseudo-English text with 60-character line wrapping:
.RS
.B gotta-go-fast -w 60
.RE
.PP
Sample code chunks from source files with a maximum height of 15 lines:
.RS
.B gotta-go-fast -h 15 src/*.hs
.RE
.PP
Practice typing prose paragraphs from text files with reflowing enabled:
.RS
.B gotta-go-fast -prw 60 books/*.txt
.RE
